From 162d2e5c11690de6bf2f178069fe5f60f9664388 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(bedrock): request live skin changes

Send a PlayerSkin update for classic skins and converted account characters while connected to a Bedrock world. Use the local actor UUID from the Bedrock player list, and keep the next-join appearance if a live update cannot be attempted. A matching server skin packet confirms the echo, but a second client is still needed to verify what others see.

Use the same negotiated Java upload path through ViaProxy and direct
translation instead of requiring client-local Bedrock storages. Preserve
complete persona, classic, animation, cape and geometry data, loading the
real bundled native skin geometry without initializing a local translator.

Correlate results with the actual Java connection and request generation.
Replacement, timeout and disconnect fail the retired request. Keep the
local preview immediate, but report synchronization only after core sees a
matching native server appearance. Remove the previous direct-only
acknowledgment path and guard character-screen status from stale replies.
